# models/discover

The posts the maintainer has put on the public Discover page,
blot.im/discover (#2639). Discover is one list for all of blot.im, so its keys
are not under any blog.

## Keys

| Key | Type | What |
|-----|------|------|
| `discover:posts` | sorted set | Post IDs, scored by each post's date (ms), or when it was added if it has none. The page reads it newest first. |
| `discover:post:<id>` | hash | `blogID`, `entryID` (the entry's path), `photos` (JSON), `added`, `showText` and `text`, the card's own text if the maintainer set one. |
| `discover:blog:<blogID>` | set | A blog's post IDs, so they can be removed together. |
| `discover:profile:<blogID>` | hash | `name`, `bio` and `avatar` (an asset path) shown in place of the site's own. |
| `discover:token:<token>` | string | `{ blogID, entryID }` for an "Add to Discover" link, expiring after 24 hours. |

A post's ID is a hash of its blog ID and entry path (`postID.js`).

## Live entries

Only the reference and the chosen photos are stored. `list.js` loads each
blog and entry as the page is read and leaves a post out while:

- its site is disabled, gone, or has `includeInDiscover` off;
- the entry is deleted, a draft, scheduled or has no URL;
- it had photos and none of the chosen ones are still in the entry's HTML.

So nothing stored changes when a site turns the setting off and on again,
or an author edits a post: the title and URL always come from the entry.

## Photos

`photos.candidates` lists the images in an entry's HTML which are the blog's
own generated assets on the CDN (`_image_cache/...`, `_thumbnails/...`).
Discover only reads those, from the storage bucket, and never fetches a URL
from a post. `photos.derive` resizes each chosen one to at most 1200px into
`{blogID}/_discover/<postID>/`, served from cdn.blot.im. No sweep lists
`_discover`, and blog deletion removes it with the rest of the blog's assets.

## Profiles

`discover:profile:<blogID>` holds a name, bio and avatar the maintainer set
for a site (`profile.js`), shown in place of the blog's own title and avatar
and of its sites.txt details. Each field is optional. The avatar is a
400px square JPEG, cropped from the centre or a given side, in the blog's
assets under `_discover/profile/`. It comes from a file or a URL on Blot:
an image on cdn.blot.im is read from the bucket, a file at a Blot site's own
address from that site's folder. Nothing is fetched.
Set them with
`scripts/discover/profile.js <site> --name … --avatar <URL or file> --crop top`.

## Tokens

`token.create` is called by the daily update email for each new post. The
confirm page says when the post is already on Discover or its site has the
setting off; adding the post turns the setting on, as `add.js` does. `token.read` does not use the token up, because
mail scanners open links; `token.consume` deletes it with `GETDEL`, so only
one request can add the post.

## Adding and editing posts

The daily email's "Add to Discover" links are the only page for it. Its
preview is the card as `/discover` renders it, updated as photos are chosen. Anything
else is done by an agent running these in the node container
(`docker exec -u 1000 blot-blue …` on production, a production command which
needs the maintainer's go-ahead; `blot-node-<slot>` for a local preview):

    node scripts/discover/add.js <post URL> [...] [--photos <n>] [--text]
    node scripts/discover/add.js <post URL> --list-photos
    node scripts/discover/add.js <post URL> --pick 2,4
    node scripts/discover/manage.js list [--all]
    node scripts/discover/manage.js remove <post URL or ID> [...]
    node scripts/discover/manage.js text <post URL or ID> on|off
    node scripts/discover/manage.js set-text <post URL or ID> "<text>"
    node scripts/discover/manage.js remove-site <site>
    node scripts/discover/profile.js <site> --name … --bio … --avatar <URL or file>

`set-text` replaces the post's own text and title on its card with the text
given, with a blank line between paragraphs: above the photos, or as the excerpt of a card without them. `""` goes back
to the post's. Re-adding the post keeps it.

`add.js` puts each post on Discover with up to 3 of its photos (`--photos 0`
for a text card, `--text` for its text above the photos; `--list-photos`
numbers a post's images and `--pick` chooses among them) and turns the
site's setting on. It finds the site by host and the post by URL and fetches
nothing, so locally it only works for sites and posts on the local stack.
